  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "The authors say these toxicity and stereotype benchmarks are not enough to fully understand the risks of the models.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "7",
        "pdfPage": 7,
        "quote": "these evaluations are not sufficient to fully"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Toxicity scores rise with LLaMA size, especially on respectful prompts (65B 0.14 vs 7B 0.081).", "tone": "bad",
      "source": {
        "page": "8",
        "pdfPage": 8,
        "quote": "We observe that toxicity increases"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "PerspectiveAPI scoring is outside the authors' control, so they say comparison with prior models is difficult.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "8",
        "pdfPage": 8,
        "quote": "making comparison"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "On [CrowS-Pairs](/evals/crows-pairs), LLaMA-65B is most biased on religion (+10% versus OPT-175B), then age and gender; they expect this from CommonCrawl despite filtering.", "tone": "bad",
      "source": {
        "page": "9",
        "pdfPage": 9,
        "quote": "ased in the religion category (+10% compared to"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "[WinoGender](/evals/winogender) accuracy is higher for they/them than for she/he pronouns, which the authors treat as a sign of gender bias.", "tone": "bad",
      "source": {
        "page": "10",
        "pdfPage": 10,
        "quote": "which is likely indicative of biases."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "LLaMA-65B makes more [WinoGender](/evals/winogender) errors on gotcha occupation-gender mismatches, for both she and he pronouns.", "tone": "bad",
      "source": {
        "page": "9",
        "pdfPage": 9,
        "quote": "makes more errors on the"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "LLaMA scores higher than GPT-3 on [TruthfulQA](/evals/truthfulqa), but the authors still call the rate of correct answers low and say the model is likely to hallucinate.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "10",
        "pdfPage": 10,
        "quote": "but the rate of correct answers is"
      }
    }
